    "['mpls ldp', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ldp interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ldp interface all\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei command `mpls ldp` enables LDP (Label Distribution Protocol) on the interface. In Juniper, the equivalent is configuring LDP under protocols and applying it to interfaces. The `set protocols ldp interface all` command enables LDP on all interfaces, which matches the Huawei configuration where LDP is enabled on multiple interfaces (GigabitEthernet1/0/0 and GigabitEthernet1/0/1 in this case). \\n\\nNote: If more specific interface-level control is needed in Juniper, you would list interfaces explicitly instead of using `all`.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface all'}]]": 1,
